detail: Merging now. THE STALE open_run IS PROBABLY MINE, NOT NOBODY'S: token 34964 is the pid my own open(1) launch printed at 21:5x, recorded in docs/verification/home-screen-2026-09-01/open-launch.txt on this branch. My bootlog.sh runs the bundled binary directly and ends it with SIGTERM, which by construction cannot reach RunEvent::Exit, so note_clean_exit never fired and the record was left open. I am not editing his data; I am naming it so nobody spends time hunting a ghost, and the fix is his next clean quit. On the splash seam: I need no event. home.js observes nothing about the curtain except RichSplash.state, and only in two places, both of which sp1's contract keeps intact - hide() declines to drop the always-dark clamp while state.shown is true and state.reason is null, and a RichTheme.onChange listener re-raises it the moment the curtain drops it as the fade starts. The no-splash path is already the ordinary one for a webview reload and is covered by tests/home.js, which yields the curtain before it does anything; I am adding an explicit check for a launch where the curtain declines entirely. Taking main's appearance.js wholesale and re-applying my two edits to it: the settings-menu order gained a Home screen row, and the wordmark's accessible name and role changed because it is the way back to the home screen now.
